# Line endings: the shell scripts in this repo must be LF everywhere.
# A CRLF checkout turns "#!/usr/bin/env bash" into "bash\r" and the script dies
# with "bad interpreter" — on Linux, in CI, and even in Git Bash through MSYS.
# So every text file is normalised to LF in the working tree, on every platform,
# regardless of what the committer's core.autocrlf happens to be.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Named explicitly because they are the ones that actually break: the entry
# script, the test harness, and the extensionless fake CLI that only works
# because of its shebang.
*.sh        text eol=lf
tests/fake/gh text eol=lf

# Markdown is prose; normalising is still right, and it keeps diffs stable.
*.md        text eol=lf

# The wizard writes the values it captures into .env files. Treat anything
# env-ish as text but never let Git try to merge it.
.env*       text eol=lf
